\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Optimization of the confining potential at fixed throat size and angular momentum. Each CMA-ES proposal starts Newton iteration from a nearby solved candidate; JAX supplies the Jacobian for the GPU solve. Exoticity, the radial screen and constraint penalties feed back into the search; inadmissible or failed solves receive a penalty. Dashed arrows lead to separate resolution and evolution tests. The loop ranks candidates; the subsequent tests assess their reliability.}}{3}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:search}{{1}{3}{Optimization of the confining potential at fixed throat size and angular momentum. Each CMA-ES proposal starts Newton iteration from a nearby solved candidate; JAX supplies the Jacobian for the GPU solve. Exoticity, the radial screen and constraint penalties feed back into the search; inadmissible or failed solves receive a penalty. Dashed arrows lead to separate resolution and evolution tests. The loop ranks candidates; the subsequent tests assess their reliability}{figure.1}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces CMA-ES exploration of the four potential parameters at fixed $R_e$ and $J$, for the drainhole (top) and symmetric (bottom) families. Panels (a,b,d,e) project recorded proposals, coloured by evaluation order; diamonds mark each search's lowest $X$ with both background-constraint residuals below $10^{-6}$. The $q_3$ axes are symmetric-logarithmic, linear for $|q_3|\le 1$. Panels (c,f) show the running minimum relative to the first candidate below that threshold. The searches concentrate in distinct parameter regions and approach plateaus at different rates.}}{3}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:search-regions}{{2}{3}{CMA-ES exploration of the four potential parameters at fixed $R_e$ and $J$, for the drainhole (top) and symmetric (bottom) families. Panels (a,b,d,e) project recorded proposals, coloured by evaluation order; diamonds mark each search's lowest $X$ with both background-constraint residuals below $10^{-6}$. The $q_3$ axes are symmetric-logarithmic, linear for $|q_3|\le 1$. Panels (c,f) show the running minimum relative to the first candidate below that threshold. The searches concentrate in distinct parameter regions and approach plateaus at different rates}{figure.2}{}}
