\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Resolution study of D21$^\star $ at $N=96,128,192$. Top two rows: Hamiltonian and momentum constraint norms through $t=50$; grey dashed and dotted curves multiply the finest-grid norms by $2^2$ and $2^4$. Bottom row: fractional equatorial- and areal-radius changes, the change in $r\,\mathrm  {Re}\,\Psi _4^{20}$ at $r=14$, and minimum lapse over each recorded history. Near-throat constraints scale approximately at fourth order early on; the later contraction begins at resolution-dependent times.}}{6}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:conv}{{5}{6}{Resolution study of D21$^\star $ at $N=96,128,192$. Top two rows: Hamiltonian and momentum constraint norms through $t=50$; grey dashed and dotted curves multiply the finest-grid norms by $2^2$ and $2^4$. Bottom row: fractional equatorial- and areal-radius changes, the change in $r\,\mathrm {Re}\,\Psi _4^{20}$ at $r=14$, and minimum lapse over each recorded history. Near-throat constraints scale approximately at fourth order early on; the later contraction begins at resolution-dependent times}{figure.5}{}}
